  Why: 'Owner 11 26: the clifftop was the weakest part of the shore: the brow strip
    stretched its grass, mixed texel sizes with the ground, and did not read as turf
    growing over and hanging off a ledge. This strip is generated at the ground''s
    texel and laid rigid on the jagged brow: a fringe over the edge, the sod mat,
    clumps of long grass hanging, the undercut, and the cut soil of the overburden
    with roots and stones.'
